senses.gloss:
धर a. bearing, supporting, wearing, carrying, keeping,
preserving, knowing, owning, possessing (—˚);
 m. a man's name;
 f. आ
the earth.

2 धा॑रा f. edge, blade (p. ˚वन्त्): margin, circumference
(esp. of a wheel);
 continuous line or series.

ध॑रण f. ई bearing, holding;
 m. N. of a
serpent-demon, m. n. a cert. weight;
 f. धरणी the earth;
 n. holding,
support, bringing, procuring.

धारण f. ई holding, bearing, maintaining (gen. or
—˚). — f. आ wearing, keeping, retaining, maintenance, assistance;
remembrance, memory;
 abstraction of mind, fixed attention (ph.);
precept, rule (j.). n. धा॑रण holding, supporting, wearing, keeping
(esp. in the memory);
 bearing, suffering;
 abstraction or concentration
(of the mind).

धरणिधर a. holding or supporting the earth;
 m. a
mountain, E. of Viṣṇu-Kṛṣṇa.

धरिमन् m. balance, weight;
 धरिममेय a. sold
(measured) by the weight.

1 धरु॑ण f. ई bearing, supporting, holding, capacious,
m. bearer, supporter;
 n. support, basis, foundation;
 receptacle (also
f.).

ध॑र्म m. statute, established order, custom, practice;
law, right, justice (o. personif.);
 good works, merit, virtue;
 nature,
character, quality, mark, attribute;
 E. of Yama & Prajāpati. — Instr.
धर्मेण according to law or virtue;
 धर्मे स्थितः abiding by the
law, virtuous. — Abstr. ˚ता† f., ˚त्व† n.

धर्मचारिन् a. virtuous (cf. prec.);
 f. ˚णी a
(virtuous) wife.

धर्मज a. begot or produced by a sense of duty;
 m.
patron. of Yudhiṣṭhira.

धर्मज्ञ a. knowing the law or one's duty;
 abstr. ˚ता
f. = seq.

2 ध॑र्मन् n. support, foundation;
 law, order, custom,
manner, modality;
 arrangement, direction;
 right conduct, duty;
 nature,
quality, characteristic (esp. —˚). — ध॑र्मणा & ध॑र्मभिस्
according to rule or nature;
 ध॑र्मणस्प॑रि in (natural) order or
succession.

धर्मपुत्र m. lawful son i.e. a son begot from a
sense of duty, also a pupil;
 *E. of Yudhiṣṭhira.*

धर्मभगिनी f. a female having the right of a
sister;
 a sister in the faith.

धर्मस्वरूपिन् a. having justice as one's own
nature or character;
 w. भगवन्त् m. Yama.

धर्माधर्म m. du. right and wrong;
 ˚ज्ञ a.
knowing r. & w.

धर्माधिकरण n. administration of the laws;
 m.
judge, magistrate.

धर्मार्थ m. du. virtue and wealth;
 ˚थम् adv. for a
pious purpose.

धर्मिष्ठ (superl.) perfectly virtuous, just, or
lawful;
 abstr. ˚ता f.

धारणक a. holding, bearing, consisting of (—˚);
 m.
debtor.

धार्मिक f. ई righteous, lawful, just, virtuous, pious
(abstr. ˚ता f., ˚त्व n.);
 m. a juggler.*

1 धार्य a. to be held, borne, worn, kept, turned, fixed,
retained, upheld, supported, observed;
 n. clothing.
